> Sorry for digging up this old post. I agree with you now, i.e. if the
> histogram is defined as having bars running from ymin = 0 to ymax = count,
> then there is no hope that you can log  transform the y axis. At the end of
> the email you find the code snippet giving rise to troubles due to my
> misunderstanding of the problem.
> What if instead (that would still be valuable to me) you want to plot the
> histogram as having bars running from e.g. ymin=1 (or 1/sum(..count..) if
> you want to normalize it) to ymax=count?

I think the easiest way around it is not to use bars - i.e. draw a
frequency polygon, which does not have the same problem unless you
have zeros in the middle of your data.

Otherwise, just set (e.g.) ymin = 1 and you should be fine.

Hadley

