Hi:

How about this? With help from the geom_histogram() help page, I came
up with the following:

gpl <- ggplot(contact,aes(x=log10(contact_data)))+
geom_histogram(binwidth=0.3, aes(y = ..density..), colour="darkgreen", fill = "white")+
# scale_x_continuous(trans = "log10")+
scale_y_continuous(limits=c(0, 0.8))+

xlab("Contact Duration (sec)")+

ylab("Pairwise Density of Contacts")+

opts(axis.title.x = theme_text(size = 20))+
opts(axis.title.y = theme_text(size = 20, angle=90))+
opts(axis.text.x = theme_text(size=15, colour="gray",vjust=1))+
opts(axis.text.y = theme_text(size=15, colour="gray", hjust=1))

BTW, the inverted histogram was really funky :)

HTH,
Dennis

